fix(ci): the operator-path gate failed on its own two files (#212)

The gate reads git-tracked files. I verified it BEFORE staging it, so it
scanned 752 files and never scanned itself, and I reported it green. Committed,
it became tracked, and CI went red on four occurrences in its own source: two
illustrative paths in the gate's WHAT IT LOOKS FOR comment and two in the
selftest's description of its fifth case.

#207's agent found it, confirmed it against 15c8f27 with its own work stashed,
and correctly left scripts/ alone because that directory is this issue's.

The comment now describes the shape in words and points at PATTERN, which is
the precise statement regardless. The selftest assembles the prefix-user name
from fragments, as it already did for its other plants.

Worth recording, because the second mistake is more interesting than the first:
the replacement comment explained why an example path cannot appear here, and
contained one while doing so. A rule that is easier to violate than to describe
is exactly the rule that needs a gate rather than a convention.

No test change. The selftest's six cases already covered this; what was missing
was running the gate after the files were tracked.

